// C14 Rust client trial: node P, not a test program: it is not externally driven and its root unit names nothing of the
// test unit. It reads the machine's clock and its stores have their own timers (once an hour, so nothing in its output
// depends on time). Its own token is valid by any present clock (variant 14). Its sentinel is a second listener of the
// Rust client. No line of this node prints a time.
// (P is built in this trial's one directory, whose unit list holds the test unit for N, as node O of
// trials/c2_tempus_clients is. The node whose build lists nothing of the test unit is node P of trials/t6_tempus_clock.)
fn port() -> string { "25601" }
fn sents() -> string { "127.0.0.1:25604" }
fn tok() -> int64 { 14 }
fn back() -> int64 { 1 }
fn blim() -> int64 { 0 }
fn fail() -> int64 { 2 }
fn driven() -> boolean { false }
fn ext_start(app: actor_ref) -> actor_ref { app }
